METHODS IN JAVA (INTRO) :
-> let us take an example of a Car.
-> We know there will be lots of functions in a car where we can say for example in programming language
    -> engine function for a car class tells the behavoiur of car's engine.
    -> seats function for a car class tells which type,len,color,number of seats of that particular car.
    -> or driving function for a car class tells the driving nature of that car.
-> In this way for a car class there are lots of functions which defines the behavoiur
   of the car parts functioning is known as METHODS(which is nthng but tells the behavoiur).

DEFINING THE METHOD BEHAVOIUR :
class Computer{
      public void playMusic(){         // void is there before playMusic method means don't return anything back
        System.out.println("Music Playing");
}
      public String getMePen(int someParameter){    //this method will do something right(behavoiur) it will return you something right!
         if(someParameter == 1){
             return "pen";
           }else{
              return "nothing";
           }
}
}
public class Demo {
      public static void main(String args[]){
// CALLING METHODS WITH OBJECTS
      Computer sys1 = new Computer();
      String str = sys1.getMePen(1);
      System.out.println(str);
      sys1.playMusic();

   }
}
